## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical data fetching with offline caching and React Native UI integration at a beginner level, using fundamental primitives like Fetch, AsyncStorage, and RefreshControl.

## Key Concepts

- Data fetching lifecycle in React hooks
- AsyncStorage-based offline caching
- Offline fallback and error handling
- UI integration with FlatList and RefreshControl
- Basic offline testing strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
import { useEffect, useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import { FlatList, RefreshControl, Text, View } from 'react-native';
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';

const CACHE_PREFIX = 'feed_cache_';

function useFeed(url) {
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);

  const fetchData = useCallback(async (isRefresh = false) => {
    if (!isRefresh) setLoading(true);
    setError(null);

    try {
      const response = await fetch(url);
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
      const json = await response.json();

      await AsyncStorage.setItem(CACHE_PREFIX + url, JSON.stringify(json));
      setData(json);
    } catch (err) {
      const cached = await AsyncStorage.getItem(CACHE_PREFIX + url);
      if (cached) {
        setData(JSON.parse(cached));
      } else {
        setError(err.message);
      }
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  }, [url]);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchData();
  }, [fetchData]);

  const refresh = useCallback(() => fetchData(true), [fetchData]);

  return { loading, data, error, refresh };
}

// Usage
function FeedScreen() {
  const { loading, data, error, refresh } = useFeed('https://api.example.com/posts');

  if (loading && !data) return <Text>Loading...</Text>;
  if (error && !data) return <Text>Error: {error}</Text>;

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={data}
      keyExtractor={item => item.id.toString()}
      renderItem={({ item }) => <Text>{item.title}</Text>}
      refreshControl={<RefreshControl refreshing={loading} onRefresh={refresh} />}
    />
  );
}
```

## Testing Offline Behavior

1. **Mock the Network**: Use a library like `nock` or React Native's `fetch` polyfill to intercept requests
2. **Airplane Mode**: Toggle airplane mode in the iOS Simulator (Cmd+Shift+2) or use Device > Airplane Mode in Android emulator
3. **Charles Proxy**: Use Charles Proxy to throttle or block specific domains
4. **AsyncStorage Inspection**: Verify cached data with `AsyncStorage.getItem()` in a separate test component
5. **Integration Test**: Use Detox or Appium to simulate pull-to-refresh while offline and assert cached data renders correctly
